.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NQSEAL 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqseal ,
.Nm nqsealwhy
.Nd seal a folder of files into a signed capsule
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqseal
.Fa "const char *dir"
.Fa "nqsalg alg"
.Fa "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "const char *meta"
.Fa "const char *tsa"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fn nqsealwhy "const char *dir" "int *why" "char *path" "size_t cap"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqseal
writes the manifest
.Pa noqtis.json
and the seal
.Pa noqtis.sig
into the folder
.Fa dir
(a UTF-8 path on every operating system), making it a capsule as
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
defines.
.Pp
It lists every entry under
.Fa dir
without following links, leaving out
.Pa noqtis.json
and
.Pa noqtis.sig
at the top; records each regular file's path, size, SHA-256 and SHA3-256
in canonical JSON (RFC 8785), sorted by path; adds
.Fa meta ;
signs the exact manifest bytes with
.Fa alg
and the secret key
.Fa sk
under the context string
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1
(pure ML-DSA or SLH-DSA, hedged); verifies the new signature with
.Fa pk ;
and only then writes both files, replacing earlier ones.
.Pp
.Fa sklen
and
.Fa pklen
must be exactly the algorithm's key sizes
.Pq Xr nqsign 3 ,
and the keys one pair: a seal that would not verify is never written.
.Pp
.Fa meta
is
.Dv NULL
or a NUL-terminated JSON object of at most 1 MiB, stored in canonical form
as the manifest's
.Ql meta
member and covered by the signature; noqtis does not interpret it.
.Pp
The creation time is the environment variable
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
(decimal seconds since the epoch) when it is set and not empty, otherwise
the clock, as an RFC 3339 UTC time to the second.
.Pp
.Fa tsa
must be
.Dv NULL .
The library makes no network requests, so it cannot obtain an RFC 3161
timestamp itself; any other value returns
.Er NQENOSUP .
To add one, build the request with
.Xr nqtsreq 3 ,
send it to the TSA, and store the reply with
.Xr nqtsput 3 ,
as
.Xr noqtis-seal 1
.Fl -tsa
does.
.Pp
The capsule and parser layers allocate through the hook of
.Xr nqsetal 3 .
.Fn nqseal
is not safe to call on the same folder from two threads or processes at
once.
.Pp
When
.Fn nqseal
or
.Xr nqseal2 3
returns
.Er NQEARG
for a folder,
.Fn nqsealwhy
says why: it sets
.Fa *why
to the first thing in
.Fa dir
that a capsule cannot hold and copies its path, relative to
.Fa dir ,
into
.Fa path
.Fa ( cap
bytes, always NUL-terminated when
.Fa cap
is not 0, cut when too long):
.Bl -tag -width NQSWLINK
.It Dv NQSWLINK
a symbolic link or reparse point;
.It Dv NQSWODD
not a regular file or folder (a device, a FIFO, a socket);
.It Dv NQSWNAME
a name
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
refuses;
.It Dv NQSWCASE
a path equal to another but for ASCII case;
.It Dv NQSWKEY
a file that starts like a noqtis secret key (its first line
.Ql noqtis-key-1 <alg> sec ) ,
which would ship with the capsule.
.El
.Pp
.Fa *why
is 0 when nothing in the folder stops a seal; the
.Er NQEARG
was then about the arguments, most often keys that are not one pair.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
(0) when both files were written, or a negative error code; nothing is
written on any error:
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Bq Er NQEARG
.Fa dir ,
.Fa sk
or
.Fa pk
is
.Dv NULL ;
.Fa alg
is unknown; a key length is not the algorithm's; the keys are not a pair;
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
is not a plain decimal number (or after the year 9999); or the folder
holds a symbolic link, a reparse point, a special file, a refused name
(empty, a control character,
.Ql / ,
.Ql \e ,
.Ql \&: ,
invalid UTF-8), two paths equal but for ASCII case, or a file that
starts like a noqtis secret key;
.Fn nqsealwhy
says which.
.It Bq Er NQELIM
More than 2,000,000 files, a path over 4096 bytes, folders more than 64
levels deep, a manifest over 512 MiB, a file over 2^53\-1 bytes, or
.Fa meta
over 1 MiB or nested more than 64 levels deep.
.It Bq Er NQEDEC
.Fa meta
is not a JSON object (strict JSON: no duplicate keys, valid UTF-8).
.It Bq Er NQEIO
The folder or a file could not be read, or a file could not be written.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation hook returned
.Dv NULL .
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
.Fa tsa
is not
.Dv NULL .
.It Bq Er NQERNG
The random source failed while signing.
.El
.Pp
.Fn nqsealwhy
returns
.Dv NQOK ,
.Er NQEARG
when
.Fa dir
or
.Fa why
is
.Dv NULL
(or
.Fa path
is with
.Fa cap
not 0),
.Er NQEIO
when the folder or a file cannot be read, or
.Er NQELIM
or
.Er NQEMEM
as
.Fn nqseal
does.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
The creation time, for reproducible capsules.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Seal a folder with a fresh ML-DSA-65 key, then check it with that key
pinned (the program
.Pa docs/examples/seal.c
of the source tree):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static uint8_t pk[1952], sk[4032];
nqrep *rep = NULL;
int rc = nqskg(NQMLDSA65, pk, sizeof pk, sk, sizeof sk);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqseal(argv[1], NQMLDSA65, sk, sizeof sk, pk, sizeof pk,
              "{\e"tool\e":\e"example\e"}", NULL);
nqwipe(sk, sizeof sk);
if (rc == NQOK)
  rc = nqchk(argv[1], pk, sizeof pk, &rep);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3 ,
.Xr nqtsput 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
